# ICCMC app · GitHub Pages deploy — ONLY the app file is tracked.
# Ignore everything, then explicitly allow just index.html (and this file).
# So no backend, worker, SQL, key or secret can EVER be committed here by accident —
# the OCR brain runs on Google Cloud Run and the data lives in Supabase, not here.
*
!index.html
# the admin OCR review page (its own self-contained build) — a 2nd app file, same rules:
# only the publishable Supabase key ships; RLS is the guard. Reached at /ocr.html.
!ocr.html
!.gitignore
# Cloudflare deploy config. Allowed deliberately: it holds no code, keys or
# connection details — only a project name, a date, and "serve this folder".
# Keep this list an allowlist; never replace it with broad patterns.
!wrangler.toml
# Tells Cloudflare which files must NOT be published. Critically it excludes
# .git — without it, Wrangler uploads the whole repo including history.
!.assetsignore
